      "message": "It looks like this also changes the behavior of cancelled asynchronous fetches.\n\nPreviously, when a cancelled async task couldn\u0027t acquire the project lock, we just logged it and returned.\n\nNow we throw `ProjectLockFailureException`, which gets wrapped in `IllegalStateException`.\n\nShouldn\u0027t we only throw for synchronous replication and leave the existing async behavior untouched?",
